## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
QCOM is a fab-lite semiconductor company, reducing its foundry dependency but still exposed to foundry capacity and pricing cycles. Its customer concentration in consumer end-markets (e.g., Apple) creates vulnerability to demand swings. Additionally, inventory digestion could be challenging given slowing consumer electronics demand.  

